400 clouds of exactly 100000 points; the annulus at 0.5. Standard errors from the spread of the clouds.
(1) raw ripple less ripple with the profile taken off, over slope^2 h^2 / (3 x points) [I had assumed +1; the referee says -1/3]:
   half-width 0.004: -0.38 (0.45)      [the slope part is 0.0074; about 802 points in the annulus]
   half-width 0.008: -0.06 (0.31)      [the slope part is 0.0149; about 1600 points in the annulus]
   half-width 0.016: -0.08 (0.22)      [the slope part is 0.0298; about 3203 points in the annulus]
